  "body": "Certifies exact local boundary minima for the existing deferred-swap CK/JP8 construction: **4 primitives for a two-cycle and 8 for a disjoint two+three-cycle**, with either arbitrary-dirty or clean workspace. The class uses the moved data coordinates plus one workspace and allows the complete PR696 primitive alphabet subject to every prefix row being zero or a signed incoming coordinate.\n\nA sign-forgetting quotient reduces the lower bound to a finite COPY/CLEAR state graph. Forward shortest paths and an independent exhaustive reverse enumeration agree; literal integer-column witnesses attain the bounds. All **168 actual boundaries** match the two classes, giving the existing **224 primitives per real component per orientation**. The prior package supplied the construction and savings; this contribution supplies the scoped lower bound.\n\nThe initial joint sign/rotation pilot ties the existing strongest comparator in all four complete cost counts. It is retained as bounded negative evidence, not a whole-run optimum or new saving. Prior sign and swap savings are not added together.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/complex-monomial-runs-seed25/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/complex-monomial-runs-seed25/verify.py\n```\n\nBoth modes check the complete certificate, eight mandatory source pins, all finite states, witness matrices, actual-boundary census, 168 affected pilot run maps and 11 rejection controls. Scope excludes temporary mixed-input rows, extra workspaces, changed run maps and physical/native admission. Paid profiles and selected kappa are unchanged; provider invoices and outer assembly were not rebuilt.\n\nCredit ToikY's retained swap-run construction/checker, Ross Richardson's PR919 sign normalizer, Sagar Thakrar's PR696 lowering, PR839's known-zero principle, Chafik Boukhalfa's PR626, Jeremy Kothe's PR622 and the retained source lineage. Prepared for **@woklerx** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance**. Apache-2.0.\n",
